pydebuprep (0.12.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New format jira-cloud: Markdown for pasting into Jira Cloud, whose editor
    shows wiki markup as plain text. Emoji carry the severity and status
    (red critical, orange warning, blue info), because a paste can't set
    text colour. The TODO list (--todo) is a table whose rows start with a
    minus sign icon for unresolved, to change to a warning sign or a check
    mark by hand. It stays within the same size limit as the wiki markup.
  * New format jira-legacy: the existing wiki markup, for on-prem Jira, pasted
    with the comment in text mode. --format jira is another name for it, so
    existing commands and configurations keep working. Use jira-cloud if you
    are on Jira Cloud. A host needs this version before a portal's config can
    set either new format; older versions reject it.
  * The labels in the report header (Host, OS, Kernel, Machine, Generated,
    Baseline and Config) are bold in the Jira and Confluence formats.
  * The report format is unchanged: portal 0.3.0 and newer take these
    reports.

